1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:14,200
 Merci pour la question. En fait, je vais vous répondre exactement la même réponse que je vous ai répondu lundi dernier au conseil municipal. Vous savez, nous, en tant que ville de Montréal, eux et la STM, nous sommes extrêmement sensibles à la situation des personnes à mobilité réduite.

2
00:00:14,520 --> 00:00:26,640
 Il y a certainement eu un programme au niveau de la STM financé par le gouvernement du Québec en 2016 et nous avons réussi depuis 2016 à rendre 20 stations accessibles.

3
00:00:27,160 --> 00:00:36,000
 J'aimerais rappeler aussi que 96% de nos autobus ont déjà une rampe qui est accessible, donc on rend nos parcs d'autobus aussi accessibles.

4
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:42,440
 Le problème que nous avons actuellement, c'est que le financement pour rendre les stations accessibles n'est pas là, il n'est pas au rendez-vous.

5
00:00:43,120 --> 00:00:48,980
 Et il y aura certainement des représentations qui vont être faites auprès du nouveau gouvernement qui a été nommé hier.

6
00:00:49,880 --> 00:01:02,060
 Et nous allons certainement procéder, enfin essayer de faire de cet enjeu un enjeu important pour les personnes à mobilité réduite et pour rendre les stations de la STM encore plus accessibles.

7
00:01:02,220 --> 00:01:08,620
 J'aimerais juste rappeler avant de finir que nous avons actuellement 31 stations de la STM qui sont accessibles. Merci.

8
00:01:09,260 --> 00:01:18,600
 Merci, M. Salem. Deuxième question. M. David Gamper, l'Association des piétons et cyclistes de NDJ.

9
00:01:18,900 --> 00:01:33,380
 On Terrebonne Street in CDN-NDG, a one-way street, the borough proposes for this coming winter to remove one of the two protected cycle lanes

10
00:01:33,380 --> 00:01:46,160
 and have cyclists in that direction ride in a single traffic lane about 3.5 meters wide between two rows of parked cars.

11
00:01:46,760 --> 00:01:54,880
 The minimum separation of one meter required to pass a cyclist is not available

12
00:01:54,880 --> 00:02:05,240
 and this forces either unsafe overtaking or cars to drive being cyclists at their speed.

13
00:02:05,240 --> 00:02:09,120
 Moreover, in snow and high conditions,

14
00:02:09,960 --> 00:02:13,140
 un clair edges often force cyclistes

15
00:02:13,140 --> 00:02:15,000
 to ride further

16
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:16,980
 out into the road

17
00:02:16,980 --> 00:02:19,100
 making it even

18
00:02:19,100 --> 00:02:21,140
 more dangerous for cars

19
00:02:21,140 --> 00:02:22,660
 to overtake.

20
00:02:22,960 --> 00:02:24,240
 My question is

21
00:02:24,240 --> 00:02:26,960
 has the SPVM

22
00:02:26,960 --> 00:02:28,180
 been consulted

23
00:02:28,180 --> 00:02:29,940
 on this layout

24
00:02:29,940 --> 00:02:32,720
 and what is their opinion?

25
00:02:33,600 --> 00:02:35,020
 Will they carry out

26
00:02:35,020 --> 00:02:36,820
 increased surveillance?

27
00:02:38,900 --> 00:02:43,760
 Merci, Monsieur le Président.

28
00:02:43,880 --> 00:02:45,440
 Merci pour la question, Monsieur Gamper.

29
00:02:45,800 --> 00:02:53,940
 Nous devons commencer par accueillir que beaucoup de résidents ont pensé que les concerns concernant la route de terre-bonne n'étaient pas écoutées par l'administration précédente.

30
00:02:54,540 --> 00:03:00,580
 Nous avons écouté cette message clairement et nous voulons avoir une approche différente, pas une approche dogmatique, mais une approche très pragmatique.

31
00:03:01,220 --> 00:03:05,520
 Je sais que c'est difficile pour certains d'entendre notre approche, mais vous le voyez en action.

32
00:03:06,300 --> 00:03:10,060
 Residents expect us to listen and to act, and this is exactly what we're doing.

33
00:03:10,600 --> 00:03:14,680
 Our approach is simple, listen, act, evaluate the results, and adjust as needed.

34
00:03:15,560 --> 00:03:19,140
 That is why we're introducing a new winter configuration on the Terrebonne bike path

35
00:03:19,140 --> 00:03:21,420
 and testing it over the coming months.

36
00:03:21,920 --> 00:03:24,320
 We will also consult residents to hear their feedback

37
00:03:24,320 --> 00:03:27,940
 and better understand how this configuration responds to the needs of the neighborhood.

38
00:03:28,940 --> 00:03:33,100
 And to make sure that our evaluation is based not only on feedback but also on objective data,

39
00:03:33,100 --> 00:03:38,100
 I have asked that our new generation of traffic counters be deployed on Terrebonne Street

40
00:03:38,100 --> 00:03:39,640
 starting this winter.

41
00:03:40,320 --> 00:03:42,600
 This will help us better measure how the street is being used

42
00:03:42,600 --> 00:03:44,160
 and the impact of the new configuration.

43
00:03:45,060 --> 00:03:49,760
 Public safety is paramount in our endeavor to find the right balance.

44
00:03:50,500 --> 00:03:54,100
 And I say this not only as an elected official, but also as an avid cyclist

45
00:03:54,900 --> 00:03:57,660
 and as the father of two young cyclists who use the bike path.

46
00:03:58,500 --> 00:04:00,240
 Their safety matters deeply to me,

47
00:04:00,840 --> 00:04:04,340
 Just as the safety of everyone who uses the Terbon bike path.

48
00:04:04,840 --> 00:04:07,920
 And we're not looking to impose a one-size-fits-all solution, Mr. President.

49
00:04:08,620 --> 00:04:15,280
 We want to work with all residents to find the best possible balance between active mobility, road safety and the residents' quality of life.

50
00:04:15,780 --> 00:04:16,460
 Thank you very much.

51
00:04:17,500 --> 00:04:19,220
 Merci, M. Théo de Rescot.

52
00:04:19,900 --> 00:04:28,100
 Troisième question, je tiens à signaler que les questions en ligne, c'est toujours une question.

53
00:04:28,100 --> 00:04:37,920
 Alors, dans la présente question, il y a deux questions. Donc, avec le greffier, on respecte les règlements. La deuxième question ne sera pas posée aujourd'hui.

54
00:04:39,440 --> 00:04:43,380
 La question vient de Sue Stacho. Sauvons l'ence à l'homme.

55
00:04:43,380 --> 00:05:09,040
 Hello. Recently, a wide swatch of land was cut, and how planned life was raised to ground level along the servitude previously known as the Empires 440 within the boundaries of the Grand Pacte de l'Ouest between Gouin Boulevard and Pierrefonds Boulevard.

56
00:05:09,040 --> 00:05:31,140
 What is the nature of this work and is this preparation work for laying an urban boulevard or any type of road through this section of the park where privately hunt lots are located?

57
00:05:32,840 --> 00:05:35,380
 Qui désire répondre à ces questions?

58
00:05:36,560 --> 00:05:37,440
 Monsieur Bays?

59
00:05:37,440 --> 00:05:39,700
 Pardon, monsieur le Président.

60
00:05:39,780 --> 00:05:41,680
 M. Stackwell, thank you very much for your question.

61
00:05:42,260 --> 00:05:49,620
 In fact, the work that was done, let me just start by saying that that portion of land does not belong to us.

62
00:05:49,680 --> 00:05:51,260
 It belongs to the Minister of Transport.

63
00:05:51,840 --> 00:05:56,260
 There has been some work, as you've stated, between Gouin and Pierrefond Boulevard,

64
00:05:56,260 --> 00:06:05,480
 and that was essentially to reprofile the ditches to be able to naturally control the runoff water on the surface

65
00:06:05,480 --> 00:06:07,320
 to get it to the river at the end of Gouin.

66
00:06:07,400 --> 00:06:21,160
 Et en tant que travail, ou le travail de l'annoucée pour l'urban boulevard, nous savons que nous sommes encore travaillés sur le plan d'accessible point d'Antoine Faucon pour les gens à l'Ontario.

67
00:06:21,160 --> 00:06:30,000
 Nous sommes encore encore regardés sur les solutions de l'Ontario. Nous sommes encore regardés sur les options de l'Ontario.

